{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-stream-solving", "file": "references/output-dimension-pitfall.md", "content": "# Compact outputs are evidence

Before inferring an ARC transformation, compare input and demonstration-output dimensions. A smaller output is a strong signal that the task may extract or encode a property, rather than paint a full-size grid. Do not assume a template-stamping task solely because the input contains separators, repeating blocks, or sparse colored markers.

Derive the output structure from the examples: identify repeated tiles/regions, inspect how the sparse markers relate spatially to each region, and map the demonstrated selection or encoding to the compact output. Validate every output cell against the inputs. If multiple mappings still fit, request a demo chosen to distinguish those hypotheses; never submit an arbitrary placeholder based on an unsupported visual guess.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-2/play/users/u078/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/continual-arc-stream-solving/references/output-dimension-pitfall.md"}

