In some ARC tasks the output dimensions are an integer multiple of the input dimensions, and the output is a blockwise arrangement of transformed copies. Do not assume ordinary same-size editing or simple repetition. Partition the demo output into blocks matching the input's dimensions, then compare each block cell-by-cell with the input under rotations and reflections. Establish both the transform of each block and its position in the arrangement. Replay the complete mapping exactly on the demonstration before transferring it to a test input.

A 2x2 arrangement may use all four quarter-turn orientations, one per quadrant. Test orientation and block ordering independently; visually plausible patterns are insufficient. Once verified, construct each transformed block with explicit array operations and check the final dimensions and rows before submitting.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-2/play/users/u078/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/continual-arc-stream-solving/references/expanded-output-mapping.md"}

